# Bidder App Backend

This is the backend service for the Bidder App. It handles all the server-side logic and database interactions.

## Development Branch

This branch is used for active development. New features and bug fixes should be implemented here before being merged into the main branch.

### Getting Started

1. Clone the repository:
    ```
    git clone -b develop https://github.com/yourusername/bidder-app-backend.git
    ```

2. Install dependencies:
    ```
    cd bidder-app-backend
    npm install
    ```

3. Set up environment variables:
    Create a `.env` file in the root directory and add the necessary environment variables.

4. Run the development server:
    ```
    npm run dev
    ```

### Contributing

1. Create a new branch for your feature or bug fix:
    ```
    git checkout -b feature/your-feature-name
    ```

2. Make your changes and commit them:
    ```
    git commit -m "Description of your changes"
    ```

3. Push your branch to the repository:
    ```
    git push origin feature/your-feature-name
    ```

4. Create a pull request to merge your changes into the `develop` branch.

